All 17 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:

**`inspector.go`** — Added `Len()` method between `Preorder` and `traverse`:
```go
// Len returns the number of AST nodes the inspector holds,
// the same count [ast.Inspect] visits over the files given to [New].
func (in *Inspector) Len() int {
	n := 0
	for i := int32(0); i < int32(len(in.events)); i++ {
		if in.events[i].index > i {
			n++
		}
	}
	return n
}
```
It counts push events (where `ev.index > i`), which equals the total number of AST nodes visited.

**`inspector_test.go`** — Added `TestLen` that verifies `Len()` matches the count from `Nodes()`:
```go
func TestLen(t *testing.T) {
	inspect := inspector.New(netFiles)
	var count int
	inspect.Nodes(nil, func(n ast.Node, push bool) bool {
		if push {
			count++
		}
		return true
	})
	if got := inspect.Len(); got != count {
		t.Errorf("Len() = %d, want %d", got, count)
	}
}
```

